{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-mghf-wjfp-p5xm","cve_id":"CVE-2026-115893","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security-advisories/GHSA-mghf-wjfp-p5xm","html_url":"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-mghf-wjfp-p5xm","summary":"Cranelift backend on aarch64 can jump to incorrect target on large Wasm `br_table` instruction","description":"# Summary\r\n\r\nWhen running with the Cranelift compiler backend on an aarch64 target, Wasmtime can compile a Wasm module with more than ~256k targets on one `br_table` instruction in a way that results in an incorrect conditional branch target. This conditional branch could then jump to arbitrary other code (at an user-controlled offset), leading to arbitrary sandbox escapes.\r\n\r\n# Impact\r\n\r\nAny Wasmtime engine running on aarch64 with default settings can be forced to jump to arbitrary code by a user-controlled Wasm module. All versions of Wasmtime/Cranelift that support aarch64, since the initial release of that support in 2020 (before Wasmtime v1.0), are affected.\r\n\r\n# Patches\r\n\r\nWasmtime v36.0.19, v48.0.7, and v49.0.4 have been released which all fix this issue.","severity":"critical","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"pchickey","id":118618,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODYxOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118618?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pchickey","html_url":"https://github.com/pchickey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pchickey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pchickey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pchickey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pchickey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pchickey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pchickey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pchickey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pchickey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pchickey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-mghf-wjfp-p5xm","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-115893","type":"CVE"}],"state":"published","created_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-23T21:28:23Z","published_at":"2026-10-19T19:21:02Z","closed_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"submission":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"rust","name":"wasmtime"},"vulnerable_version_range":"<36.0.19, >=37.0.0, <48.0.7, >=49.0.0, <49.0.4","patched_versions":"36.0.19, 48.0.7, 49.0.4","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H","score":9.9},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":null}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-691","name":"Insufficient Control Flow Management"}],"cwe_ids":["CWE-691"],"credits":[{"login":"ilyas-mallah","type":"reporter"}],"credits_detailed":[{"user":{"login":"ilyas-mallah","id":338075115,"node_id":"U_kgDOFCad6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/338075115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilyas-mallah","html_url":"https://github.com/ilyas-mallah","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilyas-mallah/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilyas-mallah/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilyas-mallah/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilyas-mallah/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilyas-mallah/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilyas-mallah/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilyas-mallah/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilyas-mallah/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilyas-mallah/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"reporter","state":"accepted"}],"collabo